WEBVTT

00:00:01.406 --> 00:00:05.058
It seems today
 that all you see

00:00:05.154 --> 00:00:08.231
Is violence in movies
 and sex on TV

00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:11.901
But where are those
 good old-fashioned values

00:00:11.903 --> 00:00:14.904
On which we used to rely?

00:00:14.906 --> 00:00:18.258
Lucky there's a family guy

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:21.911
Lucky there's a man who
 positively can do

00:00:21.913 --> 00:00:23.355
All the things that make us

00:00:23.431 --> 00:00:24.748
Laugh and cry

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:30.529
He's... a...
 Fam... ily... Guy.

00:00:35.486 --> 00:00:37.652
Wow, dinner smells great, Lois.
What'd you make?

00:00:37.729 --> 00:00:40.213
Nothing. I just defrosted
one of the casseroles

00:00:40.215 --> 00:00:42.991
Bonnie left on our porch
after my foot got infected.

00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:46.402
Most of our meals are donated
stews born of trauma.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.887
Well, I had a scary day.

00:00:47.889 --> 00:00:50.499
During my science lab,
a whole beaker of chemicals

00:00:50.575 --> 00:00:52.507
almost blew up right in my face.

00:00:52.532 --> 00:00:53.561
Oh, my God!

00:00:53.854 --> 00:00:56.338
Look at this peanut.
It's got three peanuts in it.

00:00:56.414 --> 00:00:58.748
Peter, stop bringing
snack foods to dinner.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.567
How was everyone else's day?

00:01:00.569 --> 00:01:02.408
My day was awful!

00:01:02.433 --> 00:01:04.179
I had to give
an oral book report

00:01:04.256 --> 00:01:05.347
in front of my English class,

00:01:05.459 --> 00:01:08.730
but it was right when I...
was at full mast.

00:01:08.992 --> 00:01:10.992
Okay, next up is Chris Griffin.

00:01:21.521 --> 00:01:24.263
My report is on Tom Sawyer.

00:01:24.495 --> 00:01:26.195
"A modern-day warrior,

00:01:26.328 --> 00:01:28.103
"mean, mean stride,

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.616
"today's Tom Sawyer,

00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:31.459
mean, mean pride."

00:01:31.516 --> 00:01:32.941
That is a song by Rush.

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:36.317
I don't know, man, I googled it,
and that's what came up.

00:01:36.705 --> 00:01:38.480
Well, as much as I'd love
to sit and hear more

00:01:38.556 --> 00:01:40.315
about my son's public wood show,

00:01:40.392 --> 00:01:41.583
me and the guys have a tee time.

00:01:41.608 --> 00:01:43.684
A tee time? But it's dark out.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:45.337
Miniature golf, Lois.

00:01:45.413 --> 00:01:46.654
And it's gonna be a blast.

00:01:46.679 --> 00:01:48.378
Even more fun than a Blow Pop.

00:01:49.455 --> 00:01:50.947
I never should've married it.

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:53.546
Once they say "I do,"
they don't.

00:01:57.337 --> 00:01:58.742
Ah, man, nothing better

00:01:58.744 --> 00:02:01.002
than hanging out with my pals
on a Tuesday night.

00:02:01.004 --> 00:02:04.022
Hey, why... how come we always
do stuff together on Tuesdays?

00:02:04.099 --> 00:02:07.008
It's when America unloads
all its week-old tacos.

00:02:07.085 --> 00:02:09.753
Sure, Congress can push
through "Taco Tuesday,"

00:02:09.755 --> 00:02:12.013
but we can't seem to get
decent Medicare reform.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.757
Those two things are
unrelated, Joe.

00:02:13.759 --> 00:02:15.951
Says the shill for Big Taco.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.765
Should've played through
that birthday party.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:23.458
They're playing way too slow.

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:27.375
Could we please have
some quiet on the greens?

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:37.781
Whoa, Chris, what's going on?
Where are you going?

00:02:37.783 --> 00:02:39.724
I can't take the humiliation.

00:02:39.801 --> 00:02:43.119
I think my only option is
to move away forever.

00:02:43.221 --> 00:02:45.905
What? Wh-- Is this about what
happened with your book report?

00:02:45.982 --> 00:02:47.907
The teasing was awful, Brian.

00:02:47.932 --> 00:02:50.265
Even Principal Shepherd
got in on it.

00:02:50.395 --> 00:02:51.366
Chris Griffin,

00:02:51.463 --> 00:02:53.654
please report to woodshop.

00:02:54.816 --> 00:02:55.611
Stop it.

00:02:55.636 --> 00:02:57.750
I'll stop
 when they stop laughing.

00:02:57.879 --> 00:02:59.804
My approval rating
 is through the roof.

00:02:59.829 --> 00:03:01.754
Just like Chris Griffin's rod.

00:03:03.332 --> 00:03:06.762
On a more somber note,
 that kid with the helmet die.

00:03:07.262 --> 00:03:09.579
Chris, you can't just run away
from your problems.

00:03:09.581 --> 00:03:12.415
Well, I can't just move on
and pretend nothing happened.

00:03:12.417 --> 00:03:14.417
This isn't a school shooting.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.760
Okay, I see you're upset.

00:03:16.785 --> 00:03:19.218
And I wouldn't suggest this
if it weren't so serious, but...

00:03:19.828 --> 00:03:22.516
Look, Stewie and I
built a time machine.

00:03:22.594 --> 00:03:24.355
You did? How?

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:26.279
Well, you know, I was always
really good at Legos,

00:03:26.355 --> 00:03:28.591
and I-I think it just kind of
snowballed from there.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.118
You know, if I have any advice,
it's keep building, Chris.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:33.012
Keep building.

00:03:33.638 --> 00:03:36.806
Anyway, maybe you and I travel
back in time to this morning

00:03:36.882 --> 00:03:38.576
and give you a do-over
on your book report.

00:03:38.593 --> 00:03:40.250
That would be amazing.

00:03:40.275 --> 00:03:41.550
Did Rupert come this way?

00:03:41.779 --> 00:03:43.705
Son of bitch killed his wife
and he's blaming

00:03:43.781 --> 00:03:45.039
an eight-armed man.

00:03:45.116 --> 00:03:47.208
Brian's gonna let me use
his time machine

00:03:47.265 --> 00:03:50.358
-to re-do my book report.
-Oh, is that right?

00:03:50.555 --> 00:03:53.815
And how exactly
is Brian going to do that, hmm?

00:03:53.891 --> 00:03:56.467
-With his time machine?
-Hey, I handed you a wrench.

00:03:56.544 --> 00:03:59.487
Yeah, the wrong wrench.
Just stay away from it.

00:04:05.522 --> 00:04:07.111
Hey, guys, you know
what might be fun?

00:04:07.188 --> 00:04:08.112
We should all pool our money

00:04:08.189 --> 00:04:10.173
and buy some
scratchers together.

00:04:10.175 --> 00:04:12.191
-I love that idea.
-Yeah, it'd be a great way

00:04:12.268 --> 00:04:14.026
to cap off
our Tuesday Guys' Night.

00:04:14.301 --> 00:04:17.279
Oh, speaking of that, we've got
a special on tacos today.

00:04:17.351 --> 00:04:20.016
Let's keep your politics
out of this, pal.

00:04:20.018 --> 00:04:22.185
Ah, you guys go ahead.
I'd rather spend my money

00:04:22.187 --> 00:04:24.687
on this tightly-curled
horoscope scroll.

00:04:24.689 --> 00:04:25.598
Suit yourself.

00:04:26.782 --> 00:04:29.092
Here we go, winning combo.

00:04:29.764 --> 00:04:31.322
Kim Kardashian...

00:04:31.696 --> 00:04:33.972
Khloé Kardashian...

00:04:34.087 --> 00:04:35.014
Scott Disick.

00:04:35.271 --> 00:04:37.943
I'll try my favorite,
Dignity Dollars.

00:04:38.957 --> 00:04:40.320
Martin Luther King...

00:04:40.705 --> 00:04:41.804
Malcolm X...

00:04:42.465 --> 00:04:44.816
Aww. Jussie Smollett.

00:04:44.892 --> 00:04:47.758
Let me show you how it's done.
Give me one of the Bald Bucks.

00:04:48.967 --> 00:04:49.529
Piven...

00:04:50.107 --> 00:04:51.013
Travolta...

00:04:52.847 --> 00:04:53.265
Cage.

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:54.881
-I'm a winner!
-Awesome.

00:04:54.906 --> 00:04:56.886
We won $123.

00:04:56.888 --> 00:04:59.388
Split three ways,
that's 41 bucks apiece.

00:04:59.390 --> 00:05:02.058
That's fine. I'm happy
with my horoscope scroll.

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.769
"Be sure to gamble today
with your handicapped,

00:05:04.846 --> 00:05:06.345
horny and Black friend."

00:05:06.871 --> 00:05:08.321
That-that could mean anything.

00:05:08.737 --> 00:05:10.404
"Also, close your search tabs

00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:12.944
before your big work
presentation tomorrow."

00:05:13.387 --> 00:05:14.725
Bunch of mumbo jumbo.

00:05:15.022 --> 00:05:17.147
As you can see,
third-quarter sales-- uh...

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:18.758
Oop, uh, sorry about that.

00:05:19.602 --> 00:05:20.858
Yeah, let me just, uh...

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:23.425
Okay, I-I don't know
how that, uh...

00:05:23.895 --> 00:05:25.433
Ah, just give me
one second here.

00:05:25.666 --> 00:05:27.450
A-As I was saying,
third-quarter...

00:05:28.777 --> 00:05:30.654
I apologize
for the slight, uh...

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:34.032
A mini-mart scroll warned
of this. I'll clean out my desk.

00:05:51.476 --> 00:05:52.541
I don't know, Brian.

00:05:52.543 --> 00:05:55.044
Stewie said to stay away
from the time machine.

00:05:55.046 --> 00:05:56.271
Don't worry about Stewie.

00:05:56.714 --> 00:06:01.141
Okay, just put in today's date,
set the time and go.

00:06:01.219 --> 00:06:02.568
DNA mismatch.

00:06:02.645 --> 00:06:04.328
Enter secondary voice password

00:06:04.405 --> 00:06:07.147
within 20 seconds
 to prevent self-destruct.

00:06:07.225 --> 00:06:09.079
Crap. Secondary password?

00:06:09.104 --> 00:06:10.242
Self-destruct?

00:06:10.244 --> 00:06:11.511
Wait, wait, wait. I got this.

00:06:11.896 --> 00:06:12.987
Zac Efron.

00:06:13.531 --> 00:06:15.473
Um, Susan Lucci.

00:06:15.498 --> 00:06:17.781
Uh, uh, uh, Dora. Diego.
Gold's Gym.

00:06:17.806 --> 00:06:19.552
-Mykonos.
-Oh, I-I know, I know.

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.778
Fabulous. Fab. Totally fab.

00:06:21.856 --> 00:06:23.131
Uh, uh, go, bitch.

00:06:23.541 --> 00:06:25.374
Whatever, bitch.
Love you, bitch.

00:06:25.696 --> 00:06:26.502
Um, yes, queen.

00:06:26.754 --> 00:06:27.860
Yas, queen.

00:06:27.862 --> 00:06:31.639
Y-Yas, queen.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.016
Hey. Hey.

00:06:56.448 --> 00:06:58.823
Hey. Did you see that?

00:07:08.201 --> 00:07:09.068
Check it out, Chris.

00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:11.619
Welcome to 16 hours ago.

00:07:11.906 --> 00:07:14.665
So, how does it feel
to be living in the past?

00:07:14.742 --> 00:07:17.685
Wow. Look how small
that tree is.

00:07:17.762 --> 00:07:20.081
And how old all those cars look.

00:07:20.106 --> 00:07:21.171
Oh, yeah, there's gonna be a lot

00:07:21.249 --> 00:07:22.673
of very small differences
like that.

00:07:22.950 --> 00:07:25.634
Hold on, I-I thought we were
gonna time travel to my school,

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:26.727
not to our house.

00:07:26.968 --> 00:07:28.137
Oh, yeah, I just plugged in

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:29.397
what was on the tag
on my collar.

00:07:29.473 --> 00:07:30.774
That's the only address I know.

00:07:31.613 --> 00:07:33.063
Wait a minute,
this could be amazing.

00:07:33.218 --> 00:07:35.069
We got a few hours
before your book report.

00:07:35.146 --> 00:07:37.238
And with a day's advantage,
we can use that time

00:07:37.314 --> 00:07:39.610
to bet on sports,
already knowing the outcome.

00:07:39.635 --> 00:07:41.151
Oh, my gosh, you're right.

00:07:41.462 --> 00:07:42.441
Okay, hang on, hang on, hang on.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:44.605
Ah, here we go. WNBA.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.467
There's a Mystics-Sparks game
today.

00:07:46.492 --> 00:07:47.487
Remember who won that?

00:07:47.585 --> 00:07:49.900
I don't even know
what city they're from.

00:07:49.977 --> 00:07:51.329
Which one has Caitlin Clark?

00:07:51.411 --> 00:07:52.910
I-I don't know.

00:07:53.147 --> 00:07:55.123
Both of them? Neither?

00:07:55.231 --> 00:07:56.894
Man, she's the best, maybe.

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:03.264
Hey, Cleveland.
You look different.

00:08:03.535 --> 00:08:05.324
Yeah, with my scratcher
winnings,

00:08:05.326 --> 00:08:07.887
I was able to buy
$41 of Ozempic.

00:08:08.102 --> 00:08:10.823
Donna thinks I'm starting
to look like skinny Jonah Hill.

00:08:10.848 --> 00:08:12.606
And just like Jonah Hill,
I can't wait

00:08:12.683 --> 00:08:15.851
to be an aggressively unstable
relationship partner.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:18.687
I see. Must be nice
to have money to burn.

00:08:18.764 --> 00:08:19.838
I wouldn't know.

00:08:19.863 --> 00:08:21.532
Say, guys, I forget,

00:08:21.557 --> 00:08:24.372
how many people does it take
to make a thing go right?

00:08:25.194 --> 00:08:27.771
It takes two
 to make a thing go right.

00:08:27.848 --> 00:08:29.426
I think you knew the answer.

00:08:29.641 --> 00:08:31.517
Thanks to those
lucky scratchers,

00:08:31.535 --> 00:08:34.870
I just bought Now That's
 What I Call Music! volume 12.

00:08:34.924 --> 00:08:37.549
Game, cassette, match.

00:08:37.705 --> 00:08:39.358
Hey, check it out, guys,

00:08:39.376 --> 00:08:41.284
I turned those winning
scratchers into a new belt.

00:08:41.362 --> 00:08:43.378
TJ Maxx was having a sale
on everything

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:45.531
-that's strewn on the floor.
-Great.

00:08:45.533 --> 00:08:48.217
Seems like everybody's really
enjoying their big winnings.

00:08:49.553 --> 00:08:51.934
You can't wear that shirt
because of my therapy.

00:08:53.207 --> 00:08:56.758
I got her right under
my pudgy, nonthreatening thumb.

00:09:02.066 --> 00:09:04.216
Okay, it's almost time
for your English class.

00:09:04.435 --> 00:09:06.180
We just have to head off
your past self

00:09:06.237 --> 00:09:08.237
so you can give
the book report instead.

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:10.072
Sounds good. Whoa, I guess

00:09:10.148 --> 00:09:13.375
if I have anything to say
to Derek, I should say it now.

00:09:19.328 --> 00:09:21.364
I have nothing to say to Derek.

00:09:21.702 --> 00:09:22.942
Oh, here I come.

00:09:25.681 --> 00:09:27.239
Chris, uh,
you can't go in there.

00:09:27.435 --> 00:09:29.759
Brian, what are you doing here?

00:09:32.498 --> 00:09:34.170
Are you me?

00:09:34.195 --> 00:09:36.286
Look, there's not much time.
We're from the future.

00:09:36.311 --> 00:09:38.052
Well, your future, our present.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:39.637
Let me stop you right there.

00:09:39.662 --> 00:09:41.937
I am 100% fine
with whatever this is.

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:43.459
I just go where I'm told.

00:09:45.539 --> 00:09:47.468
Okay, Chris, get in there
and make this

00:09:47.544 --> 00:09:49.544
the flaccid-est report
of your life.

00:09:49.621 --> 00:09:51.007
I won't let you down.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:54.199
Just in time, Chris. You're up.

00:09:54.201 --> 00:09:56.305
Not today I'm not.

00:09:56.384 --> 00:10:00.314
Hello, peers. This is my report
on the book Tom Sawyer.

00:10:00.499 --> 00:10:02.707
The cover shows a kid
painting a fence.

00:10:02.784 --> 00:10:06.211
And inside it is paper,
which is made from trees.

00:10:06.236 --> 00:10:08.494
- The end.
- -Chris, I may have to fail you.

00:10:08.641 --> 00:10:11.308
Well, that's all good,
'cause the only chub in town

00:10:11.385 --> 00:10:13.604
is the insurance company. Kobe!

00:10:17.817 --> 00:10:20.317
Quagmire, I see you're wearing
a brown belt today.

00:10:20.394 --> 00:10:21.707
Did you buy another one?

00:10:21.821 --> 00:10:23.821
Nope, same belt. Reversible.

00:10:24.164 --> 00:10:26.515
That just blew my damn mind.

00:10:26.591 --> 00:10:28.834
Belts are reversible,
men are becoming women,

00:10:28.836 --> 00:10:31.269
I'm kind of getting into it,
what's this world coming to?

00:10:31.355 --> 00:10:32.855
Evening, gentlemen.
Thought I'd offer

00:10:32.857 --> 00:10:36.358
some celebratory popcorn shrimp
for the big scratcher winners.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.301
Wow, no way!

00:10:37.378 --> 00:10:39.136
That's the appetizer
in commercials

00:10:39.287 --> 00:10:41.121
most likely to fly
through the air.

00:10:41.198 --> 00:10:44.308
Any food that's airborne
on television is very special.

00:10:49.995 --> 00:10:51.345
Peter, come on, have some.

00:10:51.655 --> 00:10:54.610
I understood the shrimp to be
exclusively for winners.

00:10:55.045 --> 00:10:56.320
Damn it! It's not fair.

00:10:56.455 --> 00:10:58.437
I got to find a way to have
what they have.

00:11:01.552 --> 00:11:04.144
Okay, suction cups.
Pulley system.

00:11:04.169 --> 00:11:06.630
Carabiners. Rope. Ski mask.

00:11:06.783 --> 00:11:09.129
And one last thing: a bat.

00:11:16.567 --> 00:11:19.186
I-I don't understand
the crossword ones.

00:11:23.231 --> 00:11:24.656
Well, Chris,
probably time to head home.

00:11:24.733 --> 00:11:26.658
And congrats again
on a successful,

00:11:26.735 --> 00:11:28.068
non-turgid book report.

00:11:28.145 --> 00:11:30.546
Please stop saying
gross smart words.

00:11:37.597 --> 00:11:39.531
Uh, hey... is, uh,

00:11:39.556 --> 00:11:41.270
is there maybe something
you guys want to tell me?

00:11:41.542 --> 00:11:44.326
Yeah. Did you know there was
a WNBA game yesterday

00:11:44.328 --> 00:11:46.252
between the Mystics
and the Sparks?

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:47.496
Yes, of course.

00:11:47.498 --> 00:11:49.681
The Mystics crushed
the Sparks by 26 points.

00:11:49.758 --> 00:11:50.849
Aw...

00:11:50.926 --> 00:11:53.001
Yeah, huge upset.
Vegas had it all wrong.

00:11:53.171 --> 00:11:54.336
Aw!

00:11:54.597 --> 00:11:56.096
Listen, I know
you're probably mad

00:11:56.173 --> 00:11:57.597
we took the time machine
without asking,

00:11:57.599 --> 00:11:59.842
but, trust me,
there's nothing to worry about.

00:11:59.844 --> 00:12:00.915
You sure about that?

00:12:04.931 --> 00:12:06.416
Uh, sorry, little guy.

00:12:06.696 --> 00:12:09.184
Mom thinks it'll help
the swelling from the burns

00:12:09.186 --> 00:12:11.933
if I put some of your
diaper cream on my face.

00:12:12.465 --> 00:12:14.189
Looks like Brian
 and Chris kicked up

00:12:14.191 --> 00:12:17.283
a little more than dust
 on their mosey back in time.

00:12:17.508 --> 00:12:20.712
Now, please consider
these fine commercial products.

00:12:20.789 --> 00:12:21.880
Whip sound effect.

00:12:21.957 --> 00:12:23.048
Yeah, he probably wasn't
supposed to read

00:12:23.050 --> 00:12:24.308
that last part.

00:12:24.896 --> 00:12:26.324
Yeah. There, you see?
There it is.

00:12:33.068 --> 00:12:34.735
Holy crap! What happened?

00:12:34.811 --> 00:12:37.145
We-we didn't even see Meg
in the past.

00:12:37.222 --> 00:12:38.221
Well, Brian...

00:12:38.954 --> 00:12:41.557
I would surmise that
 in the original timeline,

00:12:41.635 --> 00:12:44.216
the laughter at Chris
 emanating from his classroom

00:12:44.241 --> 00:12:45.679
created a distraction...

00:12:46.077 --> 00:12:48.690
So by turning her head
 slightly to investigate,

00:12:48.820 --> 00:12:51.320
Meg kept her face from being
 directly over the explosion.

00:12:51.984 --> 00:12:54.658
But in a timeline
where Chris was unaroused...

00:12:55.273 --> 00:12:57.199
...the distracting laughter
 was absent.

00:12:57.646 --> 00:13:00.777
Come on! Not one bag of pot
in any of these things?

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:04.189
So with no noise
 coming from Chris's classroo,

00:13:04.191 --> 00:13:06.133
Meg never turned her head away,

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:07.617
ensuring that her face
 would absorb

00:13:07.695 --> 00:13:08.969
the full brunt of the explosion.

00:13:10.407 --> 00:13:13.715
It's a weird word. "Brunt."
Such a dumb language.

00:13:13.922 --> 00:13:16.885
I feel horrible.
We got to fix this.

00:13:16.887 --> 00:13:18.689
That's exactly what
we're going to do.

00:13:18.735 --> 00:13:21.316
Oh, this is bad.
Did-did anything else change?

00:13:21.453 --> 00:13:23.625
One thing.
Lois bought popsicles for Meg

00:13:23.650 --> 00:13:25.069
since that's
all she can eat now.

00:13:29.366 --> 00:13:31.642
Mmm, so good. What's yours?

00:13:31.718 --> 00:13:33.552
-Apple.
-Aw, there's apple?

00:13:33.628 --> 00:13:34.705
I thought that was lime.

00:13:36.131 --> 00:13:36.974
But we should...

00:13:37.708 --> 00:13:40.818
we should go fix
the Meg-burned-face thing,

00:13:40.894 --> 00:13:42.302
though, right?

00:13:42.379 --> 00:13:43.970
Yeah, yeah. All right.

00:13:44.354 --> 00:13:45.489
Oh, hey, you guys.

00:13:45.566 --> 00:13:48.492
I also got ice cream
sandwiches for Meg.

00:13:49.829 --> 00:13:51.903
It's a time machine.
We can leave whenever we want.

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:53.722
I mean, we make the schedule.

00:13:53.724 --> 00:13:55.057
Yeah. Like, literally.

00:14:00.822 --> 00:14:01.890
Jon Hamm.

00:14:02.507 --> 00:14:03.609
Arnold Palmer.

00:14:04.569 --> 00:14:06.068
The third one's just a mirror.

00:14:06.427 --> 00:14:08.035
Oh, wait a minute.

00:14:08.474 --> 00:14:09.973
Scratcher!

00:14:10.050 --> 00:14:11.808
Peter? It's the middle
of the night.

00:14:11.833 --> 00:14:13.183
What the hell are you doing?

00:14:13.461 --> 00:14:16.244
-Uh... having an affair?
-What? With who?

00:14:16.344 --> 00:14:18.339
You-you don't know her.
Her-her name is...

00:14:21.145 --> 00:14:22.227
...Sandy Shoes.

00:14:22.252 --> 00:14:24.194
Peter, are you just looking
at stuff in the car

00:14:24.271 --> 00:14:25.362
and making up lies?

00:14:25.655 --> 00:14:27.589
Lois, that is completely
speedometer.

00:14:27.995 --> 00:14:29.533
Look, I don't know
what any of this is,

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:31.517
but just don't turn on
the bathroom light

00:14:31.595 --> 00:14:32.703
when you come to bed.

00:14:32.996 --> 00:14:34.520
Okay, tha-thank you.

00:14:34.598 --> 00:14:37.040
Th-Thanks for no more questions,
love you.

00:14:39.508 --> 00:14:41.027
Mr. Griffin,
you're under arrest for--

00:14:41.105 --> 00:14:43.029
I know, I know.
How'd you find me?

00:14:43.207 --> 00:14:45.482
The store security camera
caught you checking your height

00:14:45.559 --> 00:14:47.133
against the doorjamb sticker.

00:14:47.211 --> 00:14:48.560
I'm afraid I'm shrinking.

00:14:48.636 --> 00:14:50.821
We're gonna measure again
at the jail, though, right?

00:14:56.784 --> 00:14:59.237
All right, we're back at the day
of Chris's book report.

00:14:59.314 --> 00:15:01.906
To save Meg's face,
we just have to do two things.

00:15:01.983 --> 00:15:03.333
First, we lock up the Chris

00:15:03.410 --> 00:15:05.651
who successfully gave his report
without incident.

00:15:05.729 --> 00:15:08.488
-Flaccid Chris.
-Yes. Ew, ew, gross, but yes.

00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:11.381
And then we restore the laughter
that will distract Meg

00:15:11.498 --> 00:15:14.291
by releasing the original Chris
from the custodial closet--

00:15:14.329 --> 00:15:15.504
Turgid Chris.

00:15:15.906 --> 00:15:17.806
You think you're clever,
but you're not clever.

00:15:20.410 --> 00:15:22.244
Look, there's Flaccid me.

00:15:22.246 --> 00:15:24.813
Happy? Now your crudeness is
a whole thing.

00:15:26.763 --> 00:15:28.416
Okay, gonna stop you
right there, bud.

00:15:28.418 --> 00:15:30.585
Stewie? Aw, crap, this
can't be good.

00:15:30.832 --> 00:15:32.678
Hey, Chris,
we're gonna need you to--

00:15:34.258 --> 00:15:36.758
-Stewie, we've got a problem.
-What? What's wrong?

00:15:36.760 --> 00:15:38.610
It seems that, given even
a few minutes alone

00:15:38.686 --> 00:15:43.265
in a locked closet, Chris, uh...
took matters into his own hands.

00:15:43.267 --> 00:15:45.024
-What?
-Yeah, he's in there sleeping

00:15:45.102 --> 00:15:47.510
and muttering about
Lola Bunny from Space Jam.

00:15:47.535 --> 00:15:50.446
-Who's that?
-A smoking hot rabbit.

00:15:51.973 --> 00:15:54.233
Okay, I didn't get it when
you said it, but now I get it.

00:15:54.278 --> 00:15:56.702
-So, what do we do now?
-Don't worry. I've got this.

00:15:56.930 --> 00:15:58.705
Chris, your book report
is back on.

00:15:58.782 --> 00:16:01.616
But... this time you've got
to do it at full mast.

00:16:01.693 --> 00:16:03.859
Yeah, um, one small issue
with that:

00:16:03.937 --> 00:16:05.695
during the time
you two were yakking

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:08.659
about how the me in the closet
just masturbated...

00:16:08.952 --> 00:16:10.802
I, too, masturbated.

00:16:11.035 --> 00:16:12.535
-What?!
-Oh, for God's sake.

00:16:12.554 --> 00:16:14.554
Damn it! We're running
out of time to save Meg.

00:16:14.791 --> 00:16:17.349
Chris, we've got less than
one minute to get you aroused.

00:16:17.467 --> 00:16:19.467
Um... okay.

00:16:19.544 --> 00:16:22.454
Close your eyes.
You're a 19th-century heiress,

00:16:22.508 --> 00:16:23.949
alone in her vast estate

00:16:23.974 --> 00:16:26.474
and awaiting a visit
from the handsome vicar,

00:16:26.551 --> 00:16:29.461
as her dear aunt has recently
passed from consumption...

00:16:29.463 --> 00:16:31.721
Yeah, that-that's nothing.

00:16:31.866 --> 00:16:33.631
Well, I'm not proud

00:16:33.633 --> 00:16:35.039
of what I'm about
to say here, but...

00:16:35.537 --> 00:16:36.945
go to YouTube and type in,

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:40.421
"Brazilian Women's Olympic
Volleyball Team Practice."

00:16:41.007 --> 00:16:44.642
They're all speaking Spanish.
Is that part of it for you?

00:16:44.644 --> 00:16:47.662
-Portuguese, but yes.
-You guys, you guys, stop.

00:16:47.739 --> 00:16:48.813
I'll just type in

00:16:48.815 --> 00:16:51.073
"Lauren Boebert
mutual groping vaping

00:16:51.151 --> 00:16:52.317
in public Beetlejuice."

00:16:52.706 --> 00:16:55.262
Oh, you kind of sexy liar.

00:16:58.008 --> 00:16:59.641
I'm ready.

00:17:02.998 --> 00:17:04.271
He's a good kid.
I'm proud of him.

00:17:08.898 --> 00:17:10.259
What's everyone laughing about?

00:17:10.317 --> 00:17:12.166
Which one is Derek's locker?

00:17:12.263 --> 00:17:14.672
He can't find
his anti-seizure medicine.

00:17:20.034 --> 00:17:23.386
Hey, just so you know,
I can eat 50 eggs.

00:17:23.617 --> 00:17:25.725
You already told me
that four times.

00:17:25.802 --> 00:17:28.561
Okay, well, 50 sometimes
sounds like 15,

00:17:28.638 --> 00:17:31.147
so I just wanted to make sure
you were properly impressed.

00:17:31.953 --> 00:17:33.716
Huh. What are you guys
doing here?

00:17:33.718 --> 00:17:35.627
Ain't you all
too good for me now?

00:17:35.629 --> 00:17:37.311
Peter, we never felt that way.

00:17:37.388 --> 00:17:38.688
Yeah, we were
the ones who wanted you

00:17:38.764 --> 00:17:40.890
